  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 48.5% acc, while config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) achieved only 20.8% acc, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty now is whether the RNA representation itself can be improved. PCA (2000-dim linear projection) is a very basic encoder; scvi_n200 is a learned nonlinear generative encoder that may capture more task-relevant cell structure in a compact 200-dim latent space. This experiment (config_004) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001 (same singleprofile setting, only the RNA encoder changes), directly testing whether a learned encoder outperforms PCA. It is the best use of the next budget slot because the RNA encoder choice is the most fundamental design decision—it will inform every subsequent multimodal experiment and determines whether we should prioritize encoder quality or structural changes (multiprofile, aggregation) in later experiments. A large gap would shift strategy toward learned encoders; a small gap would confirm PCA sufficiency and redirect exploration toward profile structure or fusion."
}

